==In the spin-off games==
===Pokémon Puzzle League===
In [[Pokémon Puzzle League]], some available player characters include {{Ash}}, {{an|Brock}}, {{an|Misty}}, [[Tracey Sketchit]], and [[Ritchie]].

===Sega Pico series===
In [[Pokémon Advanced Generation: Pico for Everyone Pokémon Loud Battle!]] and [[Pokémon Advanced Generation: Pokémon Number Battle!]], {{Ash}}, {{an|Brock}}, {{an|May}}, and [[Max]] appear as a group. In both games, the available mini-games represent Ash's friends battling against the [[Team Rocket trio]]. In Pico for Everyone Pokémon Loud Battle!, they are referred to as Ash Team (Japanese: サトシチーム ''Satoshi Team'').

==Trivia==
* All [[first partner Pokémon]] (prior to [[Generation IX]]) have been owned by {{Ash}} or one of his friends.
* [[Alexa]] is the only human companion, main or temporary, to accompany Ash through the end of one series to the start of the next.
* {{an|Dawn}} and [[Goh]] are the only companions to share the role of protagonist with Ash during their time on the main cast.
* {{an|Serena}} is the only one of Ash's friends that Ash has met prior to [[EP001|the beginning of the series]].
* {{an|Clemont}} is the first of Ash's friends that has left the group in the middle of a journey.
* [[May (anime)|May]] and [[Max]] are the only companions that Ash did not reunite with in {{aniseries|JN}}.
* May is the first one of Ash's companions to be based on a [[player character]], while Serena is the last one of Ash's companions to be based on a player character.
* Ash's Alolan classmates are the first main characters to not appear in every episode between [[SM001|their debut]] and [[SM146|their departure]] from the main cast.
** They are also the first main characters to not appear in any [[Pokémon movie]]s.
* Goh is the first of Ash's friends to have a [[rival]]ry with one of Ash's {{Gary|former rivals}}.
** Goh is also the only one of Ash's friends to leave the group during a [[Masters Eight Tournament|major tournament arc]].
* Eevee and [[Eeveelution|its Evolutions]] are the most frequently occurring Pokémon to be caught amongst Ash's traveling companions, with four of them capturing one each, and another one being captured by two temporary traveling companions.

